      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the tables above, we have 5 degree increments between 80 and 100.  Do we want to do the same here?",
      "revId": "1d8d46c8cd9496fdcae3804f856663668fc7ddd3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26bcf5dd_3c0054d8",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/cros/thermistor/thermistor.dtsi",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 486,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-01T15:57:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like all the tables, except `thermistor_3V3_30K9_47K_4050B` include 5 degree increments starting at 80C.  `thermistor_3V3_30K9_47K_4050B` uses 10 degree increments throughout.\n\nAlso, I see upstream a preference to add the table in C code (https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/57368).  Should this be added upstream instead?\n\nIs the THERMISTOR_3V3_30K9_47K_4050B definition considered \"standard\"?",
      "parentUuid": "b9e3a7e6_00033d00",
      "revId": "1d8d46c8cd9496fdcae3804f856663668fc7ddd3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f3f5196_4fa4cf12",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/cros/thermistor/thermistor.dtsi",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 486,
      "author": {
        "id": 1530058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-01T16:20:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The compensation table is generated by the R25 and Beta values (47K and 4050B here).  The table is consistent based off of those.  I think the ideal upstream solution would be to generate this table from these inputs from reading these properties from device tree during compile time. Upstreaming tables for commonly used NTC thermistors could clutter the code base.  I created this script https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/scripts/utils/ntc_thermistor_table.py to help alleviate clutter but its now obsolete from changes to thermistor code upstream.",
      "parentUuid": "26bcf5dd_3c0054d8",
      "revId": "1d8d46c8cd9496fdcae3804f856663668fc7ddd3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "881a5086_96f10723",
        "filename": "zephyr/include/cros/thermistor/thermistor.dtsi",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 486,
      "author": {
        "id": 1529382
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-04T13:54:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with Keith. There is preference to add the tables to the C code (see https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/57368#issuecomment-1531677855). After some searching, the thermistor in our case is a MURATA NCP15WB473, which already has a compatible in the linux driver. As there is preference to align with the linux bindings, I added it to the zephyr driver together with a compensation table available from the vendor\u0027s website. I made it a part of the existing upstream PR:\nhttps://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/60682",
      "parentUuid": "8f3f5196_4fa4cf12",
      "revId": "1d8d46c8cd9496fdcae3804f856663668fc7ddd3",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    }
